            "title": "Southern California air regulators reject rules to phase out gas furnaces and water heaters",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Air quality regulators in Southern California voted 7 to 5 to reject rules that would have curbed harmful emissions from gas-powered furnaces and water heaters, but the majority voted to send the rules back to committee to be changed and reconsidered.  Burning natural gas is also one of the primary drivers of climate change.  The South Coast Air Quality Management District estimates that the rules would have lowered NOx emissions from gas-fired furnaces, preventing about 2,490 premature deaths and 10,200 new asthma cases over a 26-year period in the region.",
